Z||000000||TRiAD||10-29-2001||11:51 AM||||<I>LOL, I just realised I forgot to "flatten" this image, and lost the wheels I had put on...I'll fix that later...</I><P>Anyway, I helping a friend who owns a bodyshop do a "speedster" Miata project (no windshield, single passenger only, etc...), and it got me thinking...<BR>Should I do a Race-only Fiero?<P> <IMG SRC="http://communities.msn.com/_Secure/0RAAAAMgWSOwYZEV8FUex9GA6*9NKSI1EneLGgOsrDIL1oBDgRhms63NxNEo*TTCUQLlhw1B3obx50sNZIET9UV8HNqr!!zkQsqjaR5WaNDM/Paul-fs2-full-race.jpg"> <P>I figure; <BR>1) remove EVERYTHING not necessary<BR>2) Custom fiberglass widebody, no roof, or chopped<BR>3) Held's widebody suspension, coil-overs, big brakes, etc<BR>4) MAJOR engine mods (swap? maybe longitudinal LT1!)<BR>5) who knows...<P>So, whattdayathink?<BR><P>------------------<BR><B><I>Michael ~ triadtuning@hotmail.com</I></B><BR>-----------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88FieroGTwhitefscustomcroppedmini.jpg"> <BR><I>Photoshop rendering of planned exterior modifications.</I>||||reg||1
